        "eclairage": {
            "h2": "Street lighting",
            "lampadaires": "<b>Street lights</b>: lights recorded in OpenStreetMap, or synced from city open data. One light = one glow on the map.",
            "ruesEclairees": "<b>Lit streets</b>: streets tagged as lit in OpenStreetMap. Not every road carries that information, which is why we infer lighting for some roads from nearby street lights or from an adjacent lit street.",
            "avertissement": "An area without a glow is not necessarily unlit: more often than not, the data is simply missing. Few French cities publish an open dataset of street lights, and OpenStreetMap is not complete everywhere, especially in rural areas.",
